# Styling Conventions

## Design tokens

- All design tokens are defined in `src/styles/theme.css` using Tailwind v4's `@theme` block.
- Use semantic token names (`text-primary`, `bg-secondary`, `border-primary`) rather than raw color values or palette tokens (`gray-900`).
- Token values can be edited directly in `theme.css` — it is not kept in sync with Untitled UI upstream.

## Tailwind usage

- Build mobile-first: start with base styles, layer on responsive breakpoints (`md:`, `lg:`).
- Use Tailwind utilities for layout, spacing, and typography. Avoid writing custom CSS for things Tailwind handles well.
- When a group of utilities repeats across pages, extract it into a reusable Astro component rather than duplicating the class string.
- Avoid long one-off class strings that only make sense in one place. If a pattern is page-specific and complex, consider a scoped `<style>` block instead.

## Component extraction

- If a layout pattern (e.g., section wrapper, card, prose container) appears on more than one page, extract it into `src/components/`.
- Components should accept props for content and variants, not hardcode text or styles.
- Keep components small and focused — one concern per component.

## Custom styles

- Component-level custom styles go in `src/styles/custom.scss` (SCSS features available: nesting, variables, mixins).
- If a component's styles grow large, extract them into a dedicated file and import it from `globals.css`.
- For per-page color themes, define a CSS scope (e.g., `.theme-photo-essay`) in `custom.scss` that overrides the relevant tokens, and pass the theme class to `BaseLayout` via the `theme` prop.

## Dark mode

- Dark mode is handled via the `.dark-mode` class on `<html>`, defined in `theme.css`.
- Do not use Tailwind's `dark:` variant — it conflicts with the class-based approach.
- `BaseLayout.astro` applies `.dark-mode` automatically based on `prefers-color-scheme`.

## Images

- Photos and media that benefit from optimization go in `src/assets/` and use Astro's `<Image />` component.
- Static assets that should ship as-is (favicons, SVG logos) go in `public/`.
